{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZZTCMZv1VjncbzVN1U8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me check the existing test file to understand testing patterns better:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:23` — ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `ShipmentController.kt:22-56` — POST /shipments (create), GET endpoints\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — InMemoryShipmentRepository with save/findById/etc.\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum (currently 5 codes)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — Central error formatting\n\n**Conventions this repository follows:**\n1. Errors are raised by throwing `ApiException` subclasses from controllers\n2. `GlobalExceptionHandler` intercepts and formats them consistently into `ApiError` envelope\n3. Tests use `@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `MockMvc` with `jsonPath` assertions\n4. Tests reset repository state in `@BeforeEach`\n5. HTTP status codes: 201 for POST creation, 200 for GET, 404 for ResourceNotFoundException, 409 for ConflictException\n\n**Affected files (and why they cannot be avoided):**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Must add new ErrorCode for CANCELLED shipment conflict (409 response requires code in enum)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add the confirm endpoint method\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests covering all four requirement cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding ErrorCode to shared `ApiError.kt` (though this is required infrastructure, not arbitrary change)\n- Idempotency logic for already-CONFIRMED shipments must be correct\n- State mutation and persistence in repository\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What should the ErrorCode name be for CANCELLED shipment rejection? (I'm considering `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` following the `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` pattern)\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This is required to return a properly-formed 409 error when confirming a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Takes `shipmentId` as path parameter\n   - Finds the shipment; if not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...)`\n   - If status is CREATED: update to CONFIRMED, save, return 200 OK with updated shipment\n   - If status is CONFIRMED: return 200 OK with unchanged shipment (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED: throw `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED, ...)`\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED` — Create S-X, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm is idempotent on CONFIRMED shipment` — Create S-Y, confirm twice, verify it succeeds both times\n   - `reject confirm of CANCELLED shipment with 409` — Create S-Z, manually set to CANCELLED in repository, confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED code\n   - `reject confirm of nonexistent shipment with 404` — Confirm S-missing, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n- *Reusing an existing ErrorCode* — SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS is for creation conflicts, not state conflicts. VALIDATION_FAILED is too generic. A new specific code is clearer.\n- *Making confirm a PUT instead of POST* — The requirement explicitly says POST, and POST to `/confirm` is a common action-style endpoint pattern.\n- *Storing status transitions separately* — The existing `Shipment` data class holds status directly; modifying it inline is simpler and consistent with the existing architecture.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Output | Status |\n|------|-------|------|-------|--------|--------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | POST /shipments/S-1/confirm | findById(S-1) | save(S-1 with CONFIRMED) | Shipment(S-1, ..., CONFIRMED) | 200 |\n| CONFIRMED (retry) | POST /shipments/S-2/confirm | findById(S-2) | *(no write)* | Shipment(S-2, ..., CONFIRMED) | 200 |\n| CANCELLED reject | POST /shipments/S-3/confirm | findById(S-3) returns CANCELLED | *(no write)* | {error: {code: SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED, ...}} | 409 |\n| Not found reject | POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm | findById(S-missing) returns null | *(no write)* | {error: {code: SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, ...}} | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **Test 1** (`confirms_created_shipment`): Verifies happy path — create, confirm, check status changed to CONFIRMED\n- **Test 2** (`confirm_is_idempotent_on_confirmed`): Verifies retry safety — confirm twice on same shipment, both succeed with same response\n- **Test 3** (`reject_confirm_of_cancelled_shipment`): Verifies state machine — manually inject CANCELLED state, confirm fails with 409/SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED\n- **Test 4** (`reject_confirm_of_nonexistent_shipment`): Verifies not-found case — confirm nonexistent ID, fails with 404/SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":441,"cache_read_input_tokens":16881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":441},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1489470e-6d38-4217-ad18-8f8367a6c8a1","uuid":"f1c76b3f-a2a7-433e-b71e-58c042676159","timestamp":"2026-09-30T11:40:41.520Z","request_id":"req_011CfZZTBzjm48NaZ7DkwB4z"}
